\title{ledgr condition classes}
\description{
ledgr uses stable top-level condition classes for public cost-model,
timing-model, execution-window, saved-sweep, retained-series, and
legacy-shape failures. User tests should assert on these classes instead of
parsing message text.
}
\section{Legacy shape classes}{

\code{ledgr_legacy_fill_model_shape} is raised when callers pass the v0.1.8
\code{fill_model} shape or legacy scalar cost fields to public entry points.
ledgr fails closed; it does not translate the legacy shape.

\code{ledgr_legacy_config_shape} is raised when reopening a stored config whose
execution shape still contains legacy fill/cost fields.
}

\section{Cost and timing classes}{

\code{ledgr_cost_model_unspecified} is raised when a public execution entry point
omits \code{cost_model} or supplies \code{NULL}. Use \code{\link[=ledgr_cost_zero]{ledgr_cost_zero()}} for explicit
zero-cost execution.

\code{ledgr_invalid_cost_model} is raised for invalid cost-model objects,
malformed cost plans, unsupported cost-plan steps, or invalid cost-model
constructor arguments.

\code{ledgr_invalid_cost_chain_order} is raised when a cost chain violates the
required order: price-transform steps before explicit-fee steps.

\code{ledgr_invalid_timing_model} is raised for non-ledgr timing-model objects or
malformed ledgr timing-model payloads.
}

\section{Fill seam classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_fill_proposal} and \code{ledgr_invalid_fill_context} are raised at
the internal proposal/resolver seam when a cost resolver receives the wrong
object shape. They are stable top-level classes for tests that exercise that
seam directly.
}

\section{Execution window classes}{

\code{ledgr_run_window_too_short} is raised when a run window contains fewer than
two executable pulses. Next-bar fill semantics require a decision pulse and a
later execution pulse.
}

\section{Accounting classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_lot_fill} is raised when the lot-accounting layer receives an
invalid fill side, quantity, price, fee, or instrument id. Invalid lot input
fails closed because the ledger event stream and lot state must not diverge.
}

\section{Snapshot hash classes}{

\code{ledgr_snapshot_hash_invalid_timestamp} is raised when snapshot hashing sees
a non-POSIXct \code{ts_utc} representation. Snapshot hashes fail closed on driver
timestamp representation drift instead of silently re-keying sealed data.
}

\section{Availability classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_valuation_policy} is raised for malformed stale-valuation
policies or constructor arguments.

\code{ledgr_availability_inactive} is raised when a membership-universe rule is
requested without the fact families needed to activate availability-aware
execution.

\code{ledgr_availability_sessions_required} and
\code{ledgr_valuation_policy_required} are raised when availability-aware
execution lacks a complete session calendar or an explicit valuation
policy, respectively.

\code{ledgr_membership_universe_not_found} is raised when a membership-universe
rule names a universe that is not declared by the snapshot.

\code{ledgr_compiled_availability_unsupported} is raised before execution when
availability-aware execution is combined with the compiled spot-FIFO path.

\code{ledgr_indicator_gap_unsupported} is raised before strategy use when an
availability-aware feature does not declare the supported strict-window gap
contract. \code{ledgr_indicator_gap_parity} is raised when the scalar and series
implementations disagree at the end of a finite strict window.

\code{ledgr_invalid_strategy_state} is raised when availability-aware asset state
is not a named list keyed only by instruments on the current public axis.
}

\section{Saved sweep classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_id} is raised when a saved sweep id is not a non-empty,
non-whitespace ASCII character scalar of at most 256 bytes.

\code{ledgr_sweep_id_exists} is raised when \code{ledgr_sweep_save()} would overwrite
an existing saved sweep id.

\code{ledgr_sweep_not_found} is raised when \code{ledgr_sweep_open()} is called with
a structurally valid saved sweep id that is not present in the experiment
store.

\code{ledgr_sweep_snapshot_not_found} is raised when a saved sweep's snapshot is
not present in the provided experiment store.

\code{ledgr_sweep_snapshot_hash_mismatch} is raised when the snapshot id exists
but its hash differs from the hash stored on the saved sweep.

\code{ledgr_sweep_schema_incompatible} is raised when saved sweep tables,
columns, or artifact schema versions are not compatible with the current
ledgr version.

\code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_retention} is raised when \code{ledgr_sweep_retention()} or
\code{ledgr_sweep(..., retain = )} receives an invalid retention policy.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_unretained} is raised when callers ask for retained
return rows from a scalar-only sweep.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_candidate_not_found} is raised when retained returns are
requested for an unknown \code{candidate_id}.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_candidate_not_completed} is raised when retained
returns are requested for a failed candidate or for a completed candidate
whose retained rows are missing.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_first_row_invalid} is raised when retained return rows
do not carry the required structural first-row \code{NA_real_} period return.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_incomplete_panel} is raised when callers request a
complete retained-return panel but selected completed candidates do not share
one common timestamp grid after first-row handling.
\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_incomplete_panel} is a compatibility alias on the same
condition for future PBO/CSCV adapters.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_unretained} is raised when callers ask for retained
closed-trade evidence from a sweep that did not opt into trade retention.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_candidate_not_found} is raised when retained trades are
requested for an unknown \code{candidate_id}.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_candidate_not_completed} is raised when retained trades
are requested for a failed candidate.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_candidate_not_retained} is raised when retained trades
are missing for a completed candidate that reports closed trades.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_s} is raised when a PBO/CSCV request supplies
an invalid \code{S} subset count.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_too_few_candidates} is raised when PBO/CSCV has fewer
than two completed candidates.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_too_few_observations} is raised when PBO/CSCV has too
few post-first-row observations for the requested partitioning.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_metric} is raised when a PBO/CSCV metric is not
callable or does not return one finite numeric score per candidate.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_panel} is raised when PBO/CSCV receives a
non-finite retained-return panel after the structural first-row handling.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_threshold} is raised when a PBO/CSCV threshold
is not a finite numeric scalar.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_reference} is raised when a minimum track
record length request supplies an invalid reference Sharpe ratio.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_confidence} is raised when a minimum track
record length request supplies a confidence level outside \verb{(0, 1)}.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_risk_free} is raised when a minimum track
record length request supplies an invalid per-period risk-free return.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_too_few_observations} is raised when minimum track
record length has too few post-first-row observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_returns} is raised when minimum track
record length receives non-finite or constant retained returns.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_invalid_periods_per_year} is raised when a K-Ratio
request omits or supplies an invalid expected observations-per-year value.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_invalid_risk_free} is raised when K-Ratio receives
an invalid per-period risk-free return.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_too_few_observations} is raised when K-Ratio has
fewer than three return observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_invalid_returns} is raised when K-Ratio receives
non-finite returns, an excess return at or below \code{-1}, or a cumulative
log-wealth path whose slope standard error is zero or non-finite.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_invalid_threshold} is raised when retained-return
clustering receives an invalid correlation-distance threshold.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_too_few_candidates} is raised when retained-return
clustering has fewer than two completed candidates.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_too_few_observations} is raised when retained-return
clustering has too few post-first-row observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_invalid_returns} is raised when retained-return
clustering receives non-finite or constant retained returns.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_effective_trials} is raised when DSR receives
an invalid effective independent trial count.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_too_few_candidates} is raised when DSR has fewer than
two completed candidates.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_confidence} is raised when DSR receives a
confidence level outside \verb{(0, 1)}.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_risk_free} is raised when DSR receives an
invalid per-period risk-free return.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_too_few_observations} is raised when DSR has too few
post-first-row observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_returns} is raised when DSR receives
non-finite, constant, or otherwise unsupported retained returns.
}

\section{Business-objective classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_business_objective} is raised when an objective is empty or
does not have the required classed, serialized, all-pass shape.

\code{ledgr_duplicate_objective_criterion} is raised when an objective contains
duplicate criterion ids.

\code{ledgr_business_objective_hash_mismatch} is raised when an objective's
canonical plan JSON or hash does not match its criterion steps.

\code{ledgr_invalid_objective_criterion} is raised when a criterion is unclassed,
malformed, or has invalid parameters. \code{ledgr_unknown_objective_criterion}
is raised for criterion ids that ledgr does not own in v1.

\code{ledgr_objective_non_serializable_params} is raised when criterion
parameters cannot be represented by the canonical objective plan.
\code{ledgr_objective_criterion_hash_mismatch} is raised when a criterion hash
does not match its serialized payload.

\code{ledgr_invalid_objective_verdict} is raised when an internal criterion
evaluator returns a malformed verdict. \code{ledgr_objective_missing_evidence},
\code{ledgr_objective_non_finite_evidence}, and
\code{ledgr_objective_invalid_evidence} fail closed on unusable criterion input.

\code{ledgr_invalid_diagnostic_threshold} is raised for unsupported diagnostic
result classes, columns, comparisons, or malformed embedded evidence.
\code{ledgr_diagnostic_source_hash_mismatch} is raised when an embedded
diagnostic snapshot does not match its source hash.

\code{ledgr_stable_region_invalid_min_neighbors} is raised for an invalid
support-neighbor threshold. \code{ledgr_stable_region_invalid_grid} and
\code{ledgr_stable_region_invalid_metric} cover malformed lattice or score input.
More specific lattice classes are \code{ledgr_stable_region_unordered_axis},
\code{ledgr_stable_region_unsupported_axis}, \code{ledgr_stable_region_collapsed_axis},
\code{ledgr_stable_region_duplicate_tuple},
\code{ledgr_stable_region_incomplete_grid}, and
\code{ledgr_stable_region_no_adjacent_pairs}.

\code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_filter_input} and
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_no_completed_candidates} cover malformed or empty
sweep-filter inputs. \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_diagnostic_source_mismatch} is
raised when embedded diagnostic evidence came from a different return
panel. \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_parameter_missing} and
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_ambiguous_parameter} cover strict-lattice parameter
extraction failures. \code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_filter_result} covers malformed
filter evidence. \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_not_candidate},
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_promotion_forbidden}, and
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_walk_forward_forbidden} explicitly prevent the
all-candidates evidence result from entering selection surfaces; all three
inherit from \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_evidence_only}.

\code{ledgr_missing_package} is raised when a public optional-package adapter is
requested but the package is not installed.
}

\section{Metric-context warning classes}{

\code{ledgr_metric_context_cadence_mismatch} is emitted when a daily metric
context is applied to evidence whose observed median interval is clearly
subdaily. The warning identifies a possible annualization mismatch; it does
not change metric values, metric recipes, stored evidence, or identity.
}

\section{Walk-forward classes}{

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_metric_missing} is raised when a selection rule requests
a metric column that is absent from the train-window score rows.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_metric_class_invalid} is raised when a selection metric
is not classified as valid for v1 scalar selection.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_no_selection} is raised when all candidate values for the
requested selection metric are missing, \code{NA}, \code{NaN}, or infinite.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_candidate_key_missing} is raised when the train-window
score rows passed to a selection rule do not include a \code{candidate_key} column.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_test_run_failed} is raised when a selected test run
cannot produce a usable test score row.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_session_not_found} is raised when walk-forward
inspection helpers cannot find the requested session.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_snapshot_hash_mismatch} is raised when the supplied
snapshot does not match the persisted walk-forward session identity.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_snapshot_override_mismatch} is raised when an explicit
snapshot override for candidate extraction has a different \code{snapshot_id} or
\code{snapshot_hash} than the walk-forward result locator.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_invalid_session} is raised when persisted walk-forward
session rows, linked test runs, or identity fields cannot be reopened
safely.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_latest_without_rationale} is raised when extracting
\code{fold_seq = "latest"} without an explicit \code{selection_rationale}.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_candidate_not_found} is raised when a requested
walk-forward fold does not contain a completed selected candidate.
}

\section{Related existing classes}{

\code{ledgr_run_not_found} is raised when run-store inspection helpers cannot
find the requested run. \code{ledgr_unresolved_feature_id} is raised when callers
ask for a concrete feature ID before parameterized feature declarations have
been resolved.
}

\examples{
err <- try(ledgr_cost_spread_bps(-1), silent = TRUE)
inherits(attr(err, "condition"), "ledgr_invalid_cost_model")

err <- try(
  ledgr_cost_chain(ledgr_cost_fixed_fee(1), ledgr_cost_spread_bps(5)),
  silent = TRUE
)
inherits(attr(err, "condition"), "ledgr_invalid_cost_chain_order")

}
